    "turn_idx": 5,
    "turn_text": "I'm dealing with it was crazy because, yeah, as you say, I did. I won a very close election against an incumbent. The Republican Party didn't help me get elected. The Republican Party didn't like me. In fact, the Republicans in Washington probably liked me less than Democrats did. So for two years, I mean, again, I wasn't a 25-year-old kid who went there. I tried to get as much done as I could. I didn't want to waste time. But for a lot of people, Bill, and when you're in the house, especially, it's like you're constantly running to get reelected. And I found those two years crazy because I spent so much time trying to get reelected in two years.",
