  {
    "episode_id": 92845,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/2/92845.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 9,
    "turn_text": "It was pretty seamless for me, Dylan, because, again, when I went to Washington as a congressman, I didn't want to play around. I was serious. I slept on the floor of my office. I turned down all my congressional benefits. I turned down my health care. I wanted to get stuff done. And because I was a little different, I found myself on TV and the radio and in the media a lot. I guess I had a reputation as being very outspoken. And I did something, Dylan, that most politicians don't do. I just said, what was on my mind? And I told people what I thought. And I didn't care if it bothered people or what. But because I did that as a congressman, I got a lot of media attention because most politicians are afraid to do that kind of thing. then I lose. It was very easy for me then once I was approached to continue to do media, mainly talk radio, which I love because again, it's just me saying what I believe and having listeners call in, tell me what they believe.",
