    "turn_idx": 71,
    "turn_text": "I supported him in 2016, Dylan, because I knew why people were voting for him. And let me explain. I knew then why Trump appealed to so many voters, because the same people Trump appealed to, I appealed to. Trump's voters were my voters. Washington, D.C., Dylan back then, and I still believe now, needed some disruption. Americans, in my mind, both political parties were broken. Our politics was broken. Donald Trump ran as a disruptor. And there are good disruptors and bad disruptors. Now, I voted for him because he wasn't Hillary. I figured he's probably a goof, maybe he'll appoint a couple of good people, maybe a couple of good things might happen. I committed a big mistake, a big sin, Dylan. I did not pay attention to Donald Trump in that campaign. I did not pay enough attention to him because I did not realize what a bad person he was until after he got elected. And then when I started to pay attention to him and I realized he lies every time he opens his mouth. And then the final straw for me, Dylan, was Helsinki in the summer of 2018. when he stood in front of the world and said, I stand with Putin and not my own intelligence people. That was the greatest act of disloyalty I've ever seen in a president.",
